As SRE II, you will work closely with cross-functional teams to understand and improve the performance,
availability, reliability of Akamai's products in test network constellations. You'll define key performance
indicators (KPIs), advance the state of monitoring, alerting and investigate complex performance issue.
As a Site Reliability Engineer II, you will be responsible for:
● Deploying and maintaining the platform and software used internally by different QA and
development groups.
● Collaborating with Developers and QA teams to investigate, troubleshoot and resolve complex
problems for our stakeholders.
● Developing and implementing automated tools/pipelines to simplify and streamline frequently
seen issues and configuration change requests
● Improving our system monitoring and analysis to speed error detection, remediation, and
enhancing the performance and reliability.
● Leveraging skills in data analysis, network diagnostics, debugging tools to characterize
performance, reliability issues and recommend improvements.
Do what you love
To be successful in this role you will:
● Have 2-4 years of relevant experience and a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science,
Engineering, or related field
● Versed in one or more scripting languages (Python, Perl, Shell, Bash etc.) and familiarity with
SQL Queries
● Have Knowledge of networking protocols and technologies including TCP/IP, HTTP, DNS,
Routing protocols like BGP
● Show fluency working in a UNIX/Linux computing environment
● Experience working with network monitoring tools, virtualization technologies(Docker), Jenkins,
container orchestration like Kubernetes
● Have excellent communication skills, be able to articulate technical information in an easy to
understand manner
